<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Girl Guides & Brownies</strong>.</h3>



<div style="height:32px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Available at: </strong>KJA Kitante & Najjanankumbi.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Meeting day & time: </strong>To be announced.</p>



<div style="height:31px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At our primary school campuses in Kitante and Najjanankumbi, the Girl Guides & Brownies Club gives girls in early childhood education and beyond a space to explore, lead, and grow. Girl Guides & Brownies develop curiosity through hands-on learning, and engage in relevant activities that promote leadership, teamwork, and problem-solving skills. By participating in Girl Guides & Brownies, girls also have the opportunity to build strong friendships and support networks that can last a lifetime. Girl Guides & Brownies participate in scouting activities that can help girls build resilience and adaptability as they navigate challenges and new experiences.</p>



<div style="height:41px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Scouts</strong>.</h3>



<div style="height:37px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Available at: </strong>KJA Kitante & Najjanankumbi.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Meeting day & time: </strong>To be announced.</p>



<div style="height:33px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Our Scouts Club is open to all primary school children who are eager to learn life skills and serve their communities. By participating in Scouts, children can learn valuable skills such as teamwork, problem-solving, life skills, build lasting friendships. and communication. These experiences can help them grow into confident and capable individuals who are prepared for the challenges of the future. Scouts are encouraged to participate in community and international service projects to develop leadership skills and teamwork, and make a positive impact on the world around them. This club offers fun ways to build courage, compassion, and curiosity, all important values in early childhood education. </p>



<div style="height:40px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>



