  ('makindye', 'life', 'Safe School Environment', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Your child’s safety is our top priority. KJA Makindye operates a secure sign-in and sign-out system, ensuring only authorized individuals can collect students. The campus is also monitored by professional security personnel, providing a protected and peaceful space for learning and play!</p>', null),
  (null, 'life', 'Weekly Morning Assemblies.', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Every Friday morning, we come together for a lively assembly filled with music, prayer, and positive energy. These gatherings:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>➢ Highlight weekly announcements.</li>



<li>➢ Encourage children to lead songs, prayers, or brief presentations.</li>



<li>➢ Build confidence and public speaking skills in a warm, supportive environment.</li>
</ul>', null),
  ('makindye', 'life', 'Celebrations & Special Theme Days.', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At KJA Makindye, we believe school should be joyful and memorable. Throughout the year, we celebrate special moments that build community and create lasting memories:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>➢ Birthday Celebrations make every child feel special and celebrated.</li>



<li>➢ Sports Days encourage teamwork, healthy competition, and physical fitness.</li>



<li>➢ Fun Days Out offer exciting off-campus adventures that expand learning beyond the classroom.</li>
</ul>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li></li>
</ul>', null),
  (null, 'life', 'Languages spoken (English + Chinese + Swahili or other).', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At our school, we are proud to celebrate the diversity of languages spoken by both our staff and students. While English is the primary language used for teaching and communication, many of our teachers and children also speak a variety of local languages such as Luganda, Runyankore, Rukiga, Lusoga, Langi, and Acholi. Additionally, some staff members are fluent in French, Chinese and Swahili, further enriching our school community.</p>', null),
  (null, 'life', 'Student Leadership and Prefects.', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We believe in nurturing leadership from a young age. Our primary section has a prefect body with posts such as Head Monitor, Head Girl, Head Boy, and class prefects. These student leaders help set a good example, assist in school duties, and represent their classmates with pride and responsibility.</p>', null),
  (null, 'life', 'The 4s Club – Celebrating Achievement.', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Our reward system, the 4s Club, recognizes students who excel in academics, behavior, and participation. At the end of each term, members of the 4s Club are celebrated with a special party. It’s our way of saying, “Well done – keep shining!”.</p>', null),
  (null, 'life', 'Weekly Morning Assemblies.', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Every week begins with a school-wide morning assembly full of music, prayer, and positive energy. We share important announcements, go over the weekly agenda, and give children a chance to build confidence by leading songs, prayers, or short presentations.</p>', null),
  (null, 'life', 'Celebrations and Special Days', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We love to make school fun and memorable! At our Nursery and Primary levels, we celebrate children’s birthdays with joy. We also host exciting Cultural Days and Spirit Days like Jajjas Day, Academic Fair, and even “Wear Mommy or Daddy’s Clothes” Day! These fun events bring smiles, laughter, and a sense of belonging to our school family.</p>', null),
  (null, 'life', 'Languages spoken (English + Swahili or other).', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At our school, we are proud to celebrate the diversity of languages spoken by both our staff and students. While English is the primary language used for teaching and communication, many of our teachers and children also speak a variety of local languages such as Luganda, Runyankore, Rukiga, Lusoga, Langi, and Acholi. Additionally, some staff members are fluent in French and Swahili, further enriching our school community.</p>', null),
  (null, 'life', 'Student Leadership and Prefects', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We believe in nurturing leadership from a young age. Our primary section has a prefect body with posts such as Head Monitor, Head Girl, Head Boy, and class prefects. These student leaders help set a good example, assist in school duties, and represent their classmates with pride and responsibility.</p>', null),
  (null, 'life', 'The 4s Club – Celebrating Achievement', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Our reward system, the 4s Club, recognizes students who excel in academics, behavior, and participation. At the end of each term, members of the 4s Club are celebrated with a special party. It’s our way of saying, “Well done – keep shining!”</p>', null),
  (null, 'life', 'Weekly Morning Assemblies', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Every week begins with a school-wide morning assembly full of music, prayer, and positive energy. We share important announcements, go over the weekly agenda, and give children a chance to build confidence by leading songs, prayers, or short presentations.</p>', null),
  (null, 'life', 'Celebrations and Special Days', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We love to make school fun and memorable! At our Nursery and Primary levels, we celebrate children’s birthdays with joy. We also host exciting Cultural Days and Spirit Days like Pajama Day, Hat Day, and even “Wear Mommy or Daddy’s Clothes” Day! These fun events bring smiles, laughter, and a sense of belonging to our school family.</p>', null),
  (null, 'life', 'Teacher-to-student ratio', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">1 Teacher : 12 Pupils</p>', null),
  (null, 'activity', 'Chess', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">To strengthen critical thinking, concentration, and strategic planning</p>', 'https://kja.ug/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/1729770384619-7778.jpg'),
  (null, 'activity', 'Ballet', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">To promote discipline, creativity, and graceful movement.</p>', 'https://kja.ug/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/1748605583367-1718272521452-DSC_0976-1.jpg'),
  (null, 'activity', 'Swimming', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">To build confidence, coordination, and water safety skills</p>', 'https://kja.ug/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/1748608285694-DSC_0862.jpg'),
  (null, 'activity', 'Faith-Based Clubs', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Catechism, Islamic Studies</p>', 'https://kja.ug/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/1748607795184-PXL_20240719_081458243.MP_.jpg'),
  (null, 'activity', 'Leadership, Character & Life Skills', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Scouts, Brownies / Girl Guides, Home Management Club</p>', 'https://kja.ug/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/IMG-20250814-WA0163.jpg'),
  (null, 'activity', 'Academic & Enrichment Clubs', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Chess Club, Spelling Bee Club, Readers Dozen (Reading) Club, Traveller Club, Computer Club, French Club</p>', 'https://kja.ug/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/1729770384619-7778.jpg'),
  (null, 'activity', 'Sports & Physical Activities', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Swimming, Talent Xtra Soccer Club, Badminton</p>', 'https://kja.ug/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/IMG-20250814-WA0058-1.jpg'),
  (null, 'activity', 'Creative & Performing Arts', '<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ballet, Piano Lessons, Guitar Lessons, Music, Dance & Drama (MDD), Arts & Crafts.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>', 'https://kja.ug/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/IMG-20250814-WA0151.jpg');
